.TH TAU-CONFIG 5 "2026-10-06" "tau 0.4.0" "Tau File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
tau\-config \- tau configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fB~/.config/tau/config.json\fR (built from \fB$HOME\fR) is an optional JSON file read at startup. tau runs fine without it; behavior on load:
.IP \(bu 2
Missing file, unreadable file, or unset \fBHOME\fR \(-> all defaults are used.
.IP \(bu 2
Invalid JSON \(-> a warning is printed to stderr and defaults are used; tau does not exit.
.IP \(bu 2
Unknown keys are ignored silently, so the file is forward\-compatible.
.PP
Precedence: \fBCLI flags > environment > config file > in\-code defaults\fR. Keys set in the file become the base config; matching CLI flags override them for that invocation.
.SH "CONFIG KEYS"
.TP
\fBprovider\fR
Type: string; default: "xiaomi". CLI: \fB\-\-provider <name>\fR.
Must match a name in the provider table.
.TP
\fBmodel\fR
Type: string; default: provider's default model. CLI: \fB\-\-model <id>\fR.
See model precedence.
.TP
\fBapi_key\fR
Type: string; default: \(em. CLI: \fB\-\-api\-key <key>\fR.
Global fallback key; sits *below* per\-provider keys in precedence.
.TP
\fBkeys\fR
Type: object; default: \(em.
Per\-provider keys: {"openai": "sk\-...", "deepseek": "..."}. Non\-string values are skipped.
.TP
\fBmode\fR
Type: "text" | "json"; default: "json". CLI: \fB\-\-mode <text|json>\fR.
Unrecognized values are ignored (stays json).
.TP
\fBstream\fR
Type: bool; default: true. CLI: \fB\-\-stream / \-\-no\-stream\fR.
SSE token streaming; \-\-no\-stream for batch.
.TP
\fBthinking\fR
Type: bool; default: false. CLI: \fB\-\-thinking\fR.
Emit reasoning/thinking chunks.
.TP
\fBdebug\fR
Type: bool; default: false. CLI: \fB\-\-debug\fR.
Perf stats + tool I/O on stderr.
.TP
\fBtemperature\fR
Type: float; default: 0.7. CLI: \fB\-\-temperature <f>\fR.
Sampling temperature.
.TP
\fBmax_tokens\fR
Type: int; default: \(em (uncapped). CLI: \fB\-\-max\-tokens <n>\fR.
Output token cap.
.TP
\fBtimeout_ms\fR
Type: int; default: 120000. CLI: \fB\-\-timeout\-ms <n>\fR.
HTTP request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fBcontext_window\fR
Type: int; default: per\-provider (256000 fallback). CLI: \fB\-\-context\-window <n>\fR.
Token capacity used for the compaction threshold.
.TP
\fBauto_compact\fR
Type: bool; default: true. CLI: \fB\-\-no\-compact\fR.
Auto\-compact history when it grows too large.
.TP
\fBcompact_threshold\fR
Type: float; default: 0.5. CLI: \fB\-\-compact\-threshold <f>\fR.
Fraction of context_window that triggers compaction.
.TP
\fBcompact_keep_recent_tokens\fR
Type: int; default: 20000. CLI: \fB\-\-compact\-keep\-recent <n>\fR.
Recent tokens kept verbatim during compaction.
.TP
\fBgoal_max_iterations\fR
Type: int; default: 50. CLI: \fB\-\-goal\-max\-iterations <n>\fR.
Per\-run agentic loop cap in /goal mode.
.TP
\fBgoal_max_continues\fR
Type: int; default: 500.
Cross\-invocation continuation cap for goal mode.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
{
  "provider": "openai",
  "model": "gpt\-4o\-mini",
  "mode": "json",
  "stream": true,
  "temperature": 0.4,
  "timeout_ms": 180000,
  "auto_compact": true,
  "compact_threshold": 0.5,
  "compact_keep_recent_tokens": 20000,
  "keys": {
    "openai": "sk\-...",
    "deepseek": "sk\-..."
  }
}
.fi
.SH PROVIDERS
.TP
\fBxiaomi (default)\fR
Endpoint: \fIhttps://token\-plan\-ams.xiaomimimo.com/v1/chat/completions\fR
.br
Env vars tried in order: \fBXIAOMI_API_KEY, then PIZIG_API_KEY\fR
.br
Default model: \fBmimo\-v2.5\fR; context window: 256,000 tokens.
.TP
\fBopenai\fR
Endpoint: \fIhttps://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions\fR
.br
Env vars tried in order: \fBOPENAI_API_KEY\fR
.br
Default model: \fBgpt\-4o\-mini\fR; context window: 128,000 tokens.
.TP
\fBdeepseek\fR
Endpoint: \fIhttps://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions\fR
.br
Env vars tried in order: \fBDEEPSEEK_API_KEY\fR
.br
Default model: \fBdeepseek\-chat\fR; context window: 65,536 tokens.
.TP
\fBopencode\-go\fR
Endpoint: \fIhttps://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/chat/completions\fR
.br
Env vars tried in order: \fBOPENCODE_API_KEY\fR
.br
Default model: \fBdeepseek\-v4\-flash\fR; context window: 204,800 tokens.
.SH "API KEY RESOLUTION"
The first non\-empty value found wins:
.IP 1. 4
\-\-api\-key flag
.IP 2. 4
Config file keys["<provider>"] \(em per\-provider key for the selected provider
.IP 3. 4
Provider env var(s), in the order listed in the provider table
.IP 4. 4
Config file api_key \(em the global key
.IP 5. 4
TAU_API_KEY environment variable
.IP 6. 4
Provider built\-in key (none currently defined)
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/tau/config.json\fR
The configuration file itself.
